On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:24:29 -0700, Pat Maddox wrote:

> Add a patch on top of this stack, that does a preflight check for all of
> the binaries. I ran `just check` on beastie and it is silently failing
> because it doesn't have the commands to run.

Done, as "[PATCH 0/2] Check and document the lab-mail client's
commands" [1], on top of the v2 stack.

Patch 1 makes just check report mbsync, msmtp, and notmuch before
anything else. If any is missing, it prints a FAIL line naming the
command and its port, then the pkg install line for the missing
packages, and exits 1 without running the other checks. Those checks
hide their commands' output, which is why the run on beastie gave
failures with no cause. With a PATH lacking mbsync and msmtp, it now
prints:

    FAIL mbsync is installed (mail/isync)
    FAIL msmtp is installed (mail/msmtp)
    ok notmuch is installed
    Install the missing packages and run the check again:
        pkg install isync msmtp

just check-mail in infra/hosts/beastie already checks the packages
with pkg info, and it runs this check after them, so it gets the
preflight too.

> What command installs dependencies, or is there documentation for it? I
> don't see any.

There was none. Patch 1 of v2 added mail/isync and mail/msmtp to
infra/hosts/beastie/ports, but that list only reaches beastie through
a boot environment built from it, and nothing said so. Until beastie
runs one built since then, install them by hand:

    doas pkg install isync msmtp notmuch

Patch 2 of the new series puts that in infra/hosts/beastie/README.org,
under the ports layer. dotfiles/notmuch/README.org gives the same pkg
install line in its check section, for any host.

